    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the membership-level rule so that **level 4 requires tenure of more than 365 days**, while a newly created owner (zero tenure) never exceeds level 3.\n\n**`AssignMembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 the scoring function in the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline:\n- Raised `MAX_LEVEL` from 3 to 4 and added `TENURE_DAYS_FOR_TOP_LEVEL = 365`.\n- Added a fourth factor: `+1` when `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365`. The owner's `registrationDate` is already set upstream by `BuildOwner`, so it's available at this step.\n- Base 1, `+1` email, `+1` `namesakeCount == 0`, `+1` tenure > 365, capped at 4. A new owner's registration date is today, so tenure is 0 \u2192 the tenure factor never fires \u2192 max level 3 for a new owner.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipLevel` schema (`maximum: 3` \u2192 `4`) and description to document the tenure factor and the new-owner cap.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` (new owner with email + `namesakeCount` 0 \u2192 level 3, not 4) passes, and the rest of the suite remains green.",
