    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe tenure rule lands exactly where the other level rules already live. `AssignMembershipLevel` is a small, single-purpose class whose whole job is composing the level from independent signals, and the new tenure check is a fourth symmetric `if (\u2026) level++;` block that reads identically to the email and namesake blocks \u2014 no new responsibility is being smuggled in, and the class is not becoming a catch-all.\n\n- The `MAX_LEVEL` bump to 4 and the new `TENURE_DAYS_FOR_TOP_LEVEL` constant (named and documented) match the existing constant idiom in the class.\n- No duplication: I checked the sibling functions and there is no existing tenure/day-count helper to reuse; `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(...)` inline is the only place this computation exists.\n- Javadoc and the OpenAPI `membershipLevel` description are both updated in lockstep with the code, preserving the \"new owner never exceeds level 3\" invariant the spec calls out.\n- The null-guard on `registrationDate` mirrors the null-guards on `email` and `namesakeCount`, so the defensive style is consistent.\n\nStructurally there is nothing a maintainer of this codebase would find surprising or want reshaped.",
